 *
 * ## Completed Milestones
 *
 * ### M1 - Toolchain & Serial Output (`0.1.0-alpha`)
 *
 * **Goal:** Prove the entire build-flash-debug chain works end to end.
 *
 * | Deliverable | Description |
 * |-------------|-------------|
 * | CMake build system | Compiles bare-metal C targeting RP2350 |
 * | Pico SDK integration | SDK used strictly as HAL, no RTOS components |
 * | USB serial output | `printf`-style debug output over USB |
 * | Initial project structure | Layer directories established |
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ### M2 - Panic Handler (`0.1.0-alpha`)
 *
 * **Goal:** Establish a reliable fault boundary before any other subsystem is built.
 *
 * | Deliverable | Description |
 * |-------------|-------------|
 * | `panic()` implementation | Halts execution, emits message over UART |
 * | No silent failures policy | All invariant violations call `panic()` |
 * | Debug gate foundation | `#ifdef KERNEL_DEBUG` pattern established |
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ### M3 - Memory Allocator (`0.2.0-alpha`)
 *
 * **Goal:** A working static-pool heap allocator with corruption detection.
 *
 * | Deliverable | Description |
 * |-------------|-------------|
 * | `k_alloc` / `k_free` | Static pool allocator built from scratch |
 * | Canary value `0xDEADFACEDEADFACEULL` | Placed after every allocation, validated on free |
 * | `k_dump` behind debug gate | Full heap inspection in debug builds |
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ### M4 - Cooperative Scheduler (`0.2.0-alpha`)
 *
 * **Goal:** A working cooperative round-robin task scheduler.
 *
 * | Deliverable | Description |
 * |-------------|-------------|
 * | Task registration API | Modules register tasks via Kernel API |
 * | Round-robin dispatch | Cooperative, tasks yield explicitly |
 * | Scheduler-kernel integration | Scheduler is kernel-owned; no direct module access |
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Active Milestones
 *
 * ### M5 - IPC Primitives (`0.3.0-alpha`)
 *
 * **Goal:** Allow modules to communicate without direct coupling.
 *
 * | Planned deliverable | Description |
 * |--------------------|-------------|
 * | Message queue | Fixed-size bounded queue, kernel-managed |
 * | Send / receive API | Exposed through Kernel API only |
 * | IPC security boundary | No module may read another module's queue directly |
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ### M6 - Flash Storage / LittleFS (`0.3.0-alpha`)
 *
 * **Goal:** Persistent key-value storage backed by flash via LittleFS.
 *
 * | Planned deliverable | Description |
 * |--------------------|-------------|
 * | LittleFS integration | Filesystem mounted over Pico flash driver |
 * | Flash driver | Thin driver wrapping Pico SDK flash ops |
 * | Storage kernel API | Read/write/delete exposed through Kernel API |
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Planned Milestones
 *
 * ### M7 - Wi-Fi Scan (`0.4.0-beta`)
 *
 * Scan for visible Wi-Fi networks via the CYW43 driver.
 * Results delivered to the requesting module through IPC.
 * No network stack, scan only.
 *
 * ### M8 - Raw Packet Capture (`0.4.0-beta`)
 *
 * Put the CYW43 radio into monitor mode and capture raw 802.11 frames.
 * Frames buffered via IPC and exposed to requesting modules.
 *
 * ### M9 - Serial Shell (`0.5.0-beta`)
 *
 * Interactive command shell over UART. First Interface-layer component.
 * Commands routed to kernel via Kernel API, shell never touches drivers directly.
 *
 * ### M10 - System Stress Test (`0.5.0-beta`)
 *
 * Full system integration test. All subsystems exercised simultaneously.
 * Validates scheduler stability, memory allocator under load, IPC throughput,
 * and storage reliability under concurrent access.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Versioning Reference
 *
 * ### Format
 *
 * `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-stage.N`
 *
 * | Segment | Meaning |
 * |---------|---------|
 * | `MAJOR` | Full milestone cycle complete and stable |
 * | `MINOR` | Every 2 milestones completed |
 * | `PATCH` | >3 bugfixes, minor improvements, or doc-only changes |
 * | `-stage` | `alpha.N` / `beta.N` / `rc.N` |
 * | `.N` | Fix iteration within a stage |
 *
 * ### Stage Semantics
 *
 * | Stage | Meaning | API stability |
 * |-------|---------|---------------|
 * | `alpha` | Core subsystems still missing | APIs will break |
 * | `beta` | All planned subsystems present, testing in progress | Mostly stable |
 * | `rc.N` | Believed shippable, confirming stability | Stable |
 * | *(none)* | Tagged stable release | Stable |
 *
 * ### Version Map
 *
 * | Version | Milestone state |
 * |---------|----------------|
 * | `0.1.0-alpha` | M1 + M2 complete |
 * | `0.2.0-alpha` | M3 + M4 complete |
 * | `0.3.0-alpha` | M5 + M6 complete |
 * | `0.4.0-beta` | M7 + M8 complete, stabilising |
 * | `0.5.0-beta` | M9 + M10 complete |
 * | `0.5.0-rc.1` | Hardening for v1 |
 * | `1.0.0` | First stable release |
 *
 * ### When to Bump
 *
 * | Change type | Action |
 * |-------------|--------|
 * | >3 bugfixes, doc-only, minor improvement | `PATCH++` |
 * | 2 milestones completed | `MINOR++`, reset `PATCH` to 0 |
 * | Full milestone cycle, stable | `MAJOR++`, reset `MINOR` + `PATCH` |
 * | Core subsystems still missing | Keep `-alpha` |
 * | All subsystems present, API mostly stable | Promote to `-beta` |
 * | Believed shippable, confirming | Promote to `-rc.N` |
 *
 * ### Single Source of Truth
 *
 * The authoritative version is always `include/version.h`.
 * Never hardcode version strings anywhere else.
 *
 * Version bumps are made on `dev` and promoted to `main`. See @ref git_workflow for details.
